ine learning-based clinical decision support systems on decision-making, care delivery, and patient outcomes: a scoping review#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)#{1}":[36,37],"#Effects of machine learning-based clinical decision support systems on decision-making, care delivery, and patient outcomes: a scoping review#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[38,40],"#Effects of machine learning-based clinical decision support systems on decision-making, care delivery, and patient outcomes: a scoping review#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)#{1}":[39,40],"#Effects of machine learning-based clinical decision support systems on decision-making, care delivery, and patient outcomes: a scoping review#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[41,42]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/ZLFRZJJ8","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/LPYY4AMR?page=1&annotation=9VST6YJB","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/LPYY4AMR?page=1&annotation=H3QJLQZJ","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/LPYY4AMR?page=1&annotation=VHM27ZBR","line":36},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/LPYY4AMR?page=1&annotation=A6GQR67N","line":39}],"metadata":{"Title":"Effects of machine learning-based clinical decision support systems on decision-making, care delivery, and patient outcomes: a scoping review","Authors":"Anindya Pradipta Susanto, David Lyell, Bambang Widyantoro, Shlomo Berkovsky, Farah Magrabi","Year":2023,"DOI":"10.1093/jamia/ocad180","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"This study aims to summarize the research literature evaluating machine learning (ML)-based clinical decision support (CDS) systems in healthcare settings.We extracted the study design, care setting, clinical task, CDS task, and ML method. The level of CDS autonomy was examined using a previously published 3-level classification based on the division of clinical tasks between the clinician and CDS; effects on decision-making, care delivery, and patient outcomes were summarized.","Findings":"The most common clinical tasks supported by ML-based CDS were image recognition and interpretation (n ¼ 12) and risk assessment (n ¼ 9). The majority of studies examined assistive CDS (n ¼ 23) which required clinicians to confirm or approve CDS recommendations for risk assessment in sepsis and for interpreting cancerous lesions in colonoscopy. Effects on decisionmaking, care delivery, and patient outcomes were mixed.","Conclusions":"ML-based CDS are being evaluated in many clinical areas. There remain many opportunities to apply and evaluate effects of MLbased CDS on decision-making, care delivery, and patient outcomes, particularly in resource-constrained settings.","Limitations":"","User_Notes":""},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"3qvutg","at":1774939670245}},"smart_blocks:susantoEffectsMachineLearningbased2023a.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.06988944,-0.02603146,0.04948667,-0.01839167,0.01798615,0.02086081,0.03457506,0.08864663,0.01847232,0.00322538,0.05221344,0.01433015,0.0077989,0.02997835,0.0121975,0.02562112,0.00630887,0.03291774,-0.01333603,0.01029997,-0.01437585,-0.05902126,-0.03110821,-0.0532965,0.03434094,-0.02147193,-0.03692937,-0.04512259,-0.10576679,-0.24298416,0.06570738,0.01993752,0.08545185,0.02085529,-0.03686479,-0.01871853,-0.01077782,0.0157319,-0.00057279,-0.03062841,-0.00299867,-0.01275878,-0.0021675,-0.04191777,-0.02406804,-0.08126938,-0.03224447,-0.06743532,-0.05635533,0.03489647,-0.02620487,-0.05666081,0.03659417,0.05063362,0.02264386,0.02146361,0.01699529,0.05125634,0.03611343,0.07737723,0.0632777,0.01608957,-0.25442764,0.04921284,0.01771113,0.02332464,-0.04233023,-0.02459302,0.02452818,0.03119805,-0.04413647,0.02695349,0.04944862,0.06442118,-0.01462414,0.04386074,0.06353407,-